{"duration_api_ms":9084,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"2a7157e6-f504-4428-9e12-97299b9e38b9","total_cost_usd":0.0010658,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":736,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1399,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1021},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":736,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1399,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":736,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":736},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1281,"outputTokens":1581,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":736,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0010658,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1178,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":736,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Generally, no.** Separation is the structural default, not a guarantee.\n\n**Portfolio:** The fund is a separate legal entity (usually a Delaware statutory trust or Maryland corporation) that owns its assets. An independent custodian holds them under 1940 Act custody rules. Sponsor creditors normally have no claim to these assets.\n\n**Shares:** Shares represent interests in the fund, not claims on the sponsor. Sponsor insolvency does not cancel them.\n\n**What can still go wrong:**\n- **Commingling or fraud** can create creditor claims despite the structure.\n- **Affiliated exposures**, such as cash sweeps at sponsor-affiliated banks or securities-lending arrangements, may be at risk.\n- **Adviser, administrator, or distributor contracts** may terminate, which can delay creations and redemptions or force board action such as replacement, reorganization, or liquidation.\n- **Licenses** for index or ticker may be affected.\n\nOutcomes depend on the facts and the documents, so verify against the prospectus, SAI, custody agreement, and sponsor filings. This is general information, not legal advice.","ttft_ms":6408,"type":"result","duration_ms":7948,"uuid":"2d245827-1220-466d-8b30-eb42b2cff6a7","ttft_stream_ms":438,"time_to_request_ms":91,"first_content_frame_ms":439,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
